// D&D's Jump triples jump distance -- no BuffKind or stat hook models jump
// height in this engine. The only jump-height lever is
// Body::jump_impulse() * Stats::jump_modifier (common/src/states/utils.rs), and
// jump_modifier is only ever set by hardcoded per-body-type special cases
// (common/src/comp/stats.rs), never by a buff. Modeled with Hastened (movement
// speed) instead, as the nearest existing "make this creature more mobile"
// buff; the jump-height rider itself is dropped, not a Lane A fit.
//
// The sheet's own variant is SelfBuff, but the range is Touch and the
// description reads "the target's legs" (third person) -- D&D's Jump can touch
// any creature, not just the caster. SelfBuff always lands its effect on the
// caster only (common/src/states/self_buff.rs: `entity: data.entity`), so this
// deviates to the established touch-ally pattern already shipped for
// spare_the_dying.ron / heroism.ron / lesser_restoration.ron: a near-inert Stab
// whose attack_effect_target: InGroup redirects the buff onto whoever is
// touched. AttackSource(Melee), not AnyDamage, gates the effect -- Stab's own
// AttackDamage is hardcoded to OutOfGroup regardless of attack_effect_target,
// so an InGroup hit never accumulates damage and AnyDamage would silently
// swallow the buff (same reasoning as weave_transfusion.ron).
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 25.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Buff((
                kind: Hastened,
                dur_secs: 60.0,
                strength: Value(0.1),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Transmutation), source: Some(Primordial)),
)
